# CRAYON UI SYSTEM

## PHASE 3–6 — COMPONENT FACTORY

Continue from the existing completed Phase 0–2 foundation.

The foundation already includes:

- semantic tokens
- themes
- theme/colorMode runtime
- metadataRegistry
- componentMap
- registry validation
- deterministic component resolution
- composition schema
- renderer boundary
- build validation

DO NOT redesign those foundations unless an actual defect is discovered.

Your task now is to transform the foundation into a substantial reusable UI library.

# PRIMARY GOAL

Implement:

```text
Phase 3 — Primitives
Phase 4 — Atoms
Phase 5 — Molecules
Phase 6 — Core Organisms

```

This must result in a meaningful inventory of REAL IMPLEMENTED COMPONENTS.

Do NOT merely add planned registry entries.

Do NOT generate empty folders.

Do NOT create dashboard pages yet.

Do NOT create blocks/templates yet except when strictly required to test composition.

The goal is:

> BUILD THE CRAYON COMPONENT INVENTORY.

---

# 1. IMPORTANT IMPLEMENTATION RULE

For every implemented component:

```text
implementation
+
export
+
registry metadata
+
componentMap registration
+
validation
+
basic demo/test where useful

```

must stay synchronized.

An implemented component without registry metadata is incomplete.

A metadata entry marked implemented without a real component is invalid.

---

# 2. COMPONENT LIFECYCLE

Use:

```text
planned
experimental
stable
deprecated

```

For this phase:

new functional components may initially be:

```text
experimental

```

After successfully passing required validation and being used consistently, they may become:

```text
stable

```

Do not mark unfinished components as stable.

---

# 3. NO ARTIFICIAL COMPONENT COUNT

Do NOT split a component merely to increase the number of files.

Atomicity must improve:

```text
reuse
clarity
composition
maintainability

```

Do NOT create things such as:

```text
ButtonText
ButtonIconWrapper
CardPadding
InputBorder

```

unless they solve a real reusable architectural need.

---

# 4. EXISTING SHADCN COMPONENT AUDIT

The project already contains:

```text
components/ui/button.tsx

```

First inspect it.

Decide the canonical ownership strategy.

Preferred direction:

```text
shadcn/Radix
     ↓
implementation primitive
     ↓
Crayon canonical component API
     ↓
registry

```

Do NOT maintain two independent Button implementations.

If migration is necessary, preserve compatibility where practical.

All NEW Crayon source should use:

```text
JavaScript
JSX

```

Do not unnecessarily migrate unrelated Next.js TS/TSX infrastructure.

---

# 5. SHADCN POLICY

Reuse shadcn/Radix primitives when they provide mature behavior for:

```text
Dialog
Popover
Tooltip
Dropdown
Select
Tabs
Accordion
Checkbox
Radio
Switch
Command
ScrollArea
Separator
Avatar

```

Do not rewrite accessibility-sensitive primitives poorly.

However:

> Crayon owns the public component API.

Do not expose random inconsistent generated shadcn components directly throughout the application.

Normalize them through the Crayon component system where necessary.

---

# 6. PHASE 3 — PRIMITIVES

Implement a meaningful primitive layer.

Candidates:

```text
Box
Stack
Inline
Cluster
Container
Surface
Text
Heading
Separator
ScrollArea
AspectRatio
VisuallyHidden
Portal
FocusRing

```

Do not implement a primitive if native HTML/CSS composition already solves the problem clearly.

Expected useful primitive inventory:

approximately 8–14 components.

Each primitive must:

- be domain-neutral
- contain no business logic
- contain no hardcoded application data
- support className
- support sensible HTML semantics
- support composition
- use Crayon tokens
- remain theme-compatible

---

# 7. STACK

Implement a reusable Stack primitive.

Expected conceptual API:

```jsx
<Stack
  gap="md"
  align="stretch"
>
  ...
</Stack>

```

Do not allow arbitrary styling APIs to replace Tailwind/CSS completely.

Only expose meaningful structural options.

---

# 8. INLINE

Provide horizontal composition.

Example:

```jsx
<Inline
  gap="sm"
  align="center"
  wrap
>
  ...
</Inline>

```

---

# 9. CONTAINER

Provide consistent content width and horizontal page padding.

Support sensible size variants such as:

```text
sm
md
lg
xl
full

```

Do not hardcode a width for one application.

---

# 10. SURFACE

Surface represents semantic elevation/background hierarchy.

Possible variants:

```text
default
subtle
raised
overlay
interactive

```

Themes determine actual appearance.

Do not create:

```text
GlassSurface
ObsidianSurface
CorporateSurface

```

---

# 11. TEXT AND HEADING

Provide semantic typography components only if they materially improve consistency.

Support semantic HTML.

Do not create a giant typography abstraction with dozens of arbitrary props.

---

# 12. PHASE 4 — ATOMS

Build the canonical Crayon atom inventory.

Target approximately:

```text
20–30 useful atoms

```

Candidates:

```text
Button
IconButton
Input
Textarea
Label
Checkbox
Radio
RadioGroup
Switch
Select
Badge
StatusBadge
StatusDot
Avatar
Icon
Spinner
Progress
Skeleton
Divider
Link
Kbd
Chip
Counter
Tooltip
Code
CopyButton

```

Only keep meaningful distinctions.

---

# 13. BUTTON

Create ONE canonical Button.

Expected variants:

```text
default
secondary
outline
ghost
destructive
link

```

Expected sizes:

```text
xs
sm
md
lg
icon

```

Required states:

```text
default
hover
focus
active
disabled
loading

```

Support icons through composition.

Example:

```jsx
<Button>
  Save
</Button>

```

and:

```jsx
<Button>
  <SaveIcon />
  Save
</Button>

```

Loading state should not require a separate LoadingButton component.

---

# 14. ICON BUTTON

IconButton should exist only because icon-only controls require:

```text
accessible labeling
square sizing
consistent focus behavior
tooltip compatibility

```

Require accessible name through:

```text
aria-label

```

or equivalent.

---

# 15. INPUT FAMILY

Implement coherent:

```text
Input
Textarea
Select
Checkbox
Radio
Switch

```

They must use shared:

```text
focus
disabled
invalid
size
surface
border

```

design language.

Do not individually invent styling for every input.

---

# 16. BADGES

Avoid creating too many badge components.

Prefer:

```jsx
<Badge variant="success" />

```

rather than:

```text
SuccessBadge
WarningBadge
ErrorBadge
InfoBadge

```

StatusBadge may remain separate only if it combines semantic status logic/icons beyond plain Badge behavior.

---

# 17. LOADING ATOMS

Implement reusable:

```text
Spinner
Progress
Skeleton

```

Respect reduced motion.

Loading state should not cause large layout shifts.

---

# 18. TOOLTIP

Use an accessible primitive.

Tooltip must work with:

```text
mouse
keyboard focus

```

Do not use title attributes as the only tooltip implementation.

---

# 19. COPY BUTTON

Implement a useful generic CopyButton.

Accept content/value externally.

Do not hardcode clipboard messages that cannot be localized.

---

# 20. PHASE 5 — MOLECULES

Build approximately:

```text
20–35 molecules

```

Candidates:

```text
FormField
SearchInput
PasswordInput
FilterChip
Breadcrumb
Pagination
UserMenu
ThemeSwitcher
ColorModeSwitcher
NotificationItem
StatValue
TrendIndicator
MetricSummary
EmptyState
ErrorState
LoadingState
FileDropzone
CopyField
CommandItem
NavItem
PropertyRow
KeyValue
AvatarGroup
SearchField
ActionMenu
PageActions
StatusLabel
FieldGroup
InputWithAction
DateInput
TimeInput

```

Do not blindly implement every candidate.

Audit overlap before implementation.

---

# 21. FORM FIELD

Create a canonical FormField composition.

Concept:

```jsx
<FormField
  label="Email"
  description="Used for notifications."
  error={error}
  required
>
  <Input />
</FormField>

```

It should manage:

```text
label relationship
description relationship
error relationship
spacing
required state

```

without depending on React Hook Form or another specific validation library.

---

# 22. SEARCH INPUT

Compose Input + icon + optional clear action.

Expected API concept:

```jsx
<SearchInput
  value={query}
  onChange={...}
  onClear={...}
  placeholder="Search..."
/>

```

No API requests inside SearchInput.

---

# 23. PASSWORD INPUT

Compose Input + visibility toggle.

Accessibility is mandatory.

Do not add authentication logic.

---

# 24. EMPTY STATE

Canonical reusable empty-state composition:

```jsx
<EmptyState
  icon={Inbox}
  title="No results"
  description="Try changing your filters."
  action={<Button>Reset filters</Button>}
/>

```

No hardcoded domain text.

---

# 25. ERROR STATE

Support:

```text
title
description
error code if supplied
retry action
secondary action

```

Do not expose stack traces automatically.

---

# 26. PAGINATION

Keep it data-source independent.

Accept values such as:

```text
page
pageCount
onPageChange

```

Do not construct backend URLs itself.

---

# 27. BREADCRUMB

Breadcrumb data should be injected.

Do not assume Next.js routing internally.

Allow app-level link rendering where needed.

---

# 28. NAV ITEM

Create canonical navigation-item behavior reused by:

```text
sidebar
top navigation
command navigation

```

where appropriate.

Do not over-generalize if interaction models materially differ.

---

# 29. PROPERTY ROW / KEY VALUE

Useful for technical and enterprise UIs.

Example:

```jsx
<KeyValue
  label="Region"
  value="Jakarta"
/>

```

Values remain arbitrary React content where appropriate.

---

# 30. STAT VALUE

Create a domain-neutral metric display primitive/molecule.

Example:

```jsx
<StatValue
  value={value}
  label={label}
  change={change}
/>

```

Do NOT call it RevenueStat or UserStat.

---

# 31. TREND INDICATOR

Provide:

```text
up
down
neutral

```

Avoid assuming:

```text
up = always good
down = always bad

```

Allow semantic interpretation:

```text
positive
negative
neutral

```

to be injected.

This matters for metrics such as latency/error rate.

---

# 32. PHASE 6 — CORE ORGANISMS

After primitives, atoms, and molecules are stable enough, implement approximately:

```text
12–20 core organisms

```

Focus on reusable application structure.

Candidates:

```text
PageHeader
Sidebar
Topbar
DataTable
FilterBar
CommandPalette
NotificationPanel
ActivityFeed
MetricGrid
ChartPanel
FormSection
SettingsSection
DetailPanel
DrawerPanel
Timeline
FileBrowser
TreeView
InspectorPanel

```

Prioritize components that will later enable many blocks/templates.

---

# 33. PAGE HEADER

Support:

```text
title
description
breadcrumbs
actions
metadata

```

through composition.

No application-specific titles.

---

# 34. SIDEBAR

Build a robust reusable Sidebar.

Support:

```text
navigation groups
navigation items
icons
badges
active state
collapsed state
header
footer
mobile drawer mode

```

Navigation must be injected.

Never hardcode:

```text
Dashboard
CRM
Billing
Settings

```

inside Sidebar.

---

# 35. TOPBAR

Support slots such as:

```text
leading
center
actions
userMenu

```

Keep route/business logic external.

---

# 36. DATA TABLE

This is a critical Crayon organism.

Build a reusable table API.

Support, where practical:

```text
columns
data
row key
sorting
row selection
pagination boundary
loading
empty
error
row actions
bulk actions
column visibility
density
sticky header

```

Do not create a full enterprise spreadsheet engine.

Avoid premature complexity.

Domain wrappers will come later.

---

# 37. FILTER BAR

Compose:

```text
search
filters
active filters
clear/reset
actions

```

without knowing backend query syntax.

---

# 38. COMMAND PALETTE

Use accessible keyboard interaction.

Its items/actions are injected.

No hardcoded Crayon commands.

---

# 39. NOTIFICATION PANEL

Accept notification data externally.

Support:

```text
read/unread
timestamp
icon
action
empty state

```

No networking.

---

# 40. ACTIVITY FEED

Generic reusable feed supporting:

```text
actor
action
subject
timestamp
metadata
icon

```

Do not assume CRM or GitHub specifically.

---

# 41. METRIC GRID

MetricGrid should primarily compose repeated metric/stat components.

Responsive layout should be automatic and predictable.

---

# 42. FORM SECTION

Reusable settings/form grouping.

Example:

```jsx
<FormSection
  title="Profile"
  description="..."
>
  ...
</FormSection>

```

No form submission/business logic.

---

# 43. DETAIL PANEL

Useful for:

```text
CRM
ERP
infrastructure
projects
AI tool output

```

Support sections/slots without becoming a giant schema.

---

# 44. COMPONENT REGISTRY REQUIREMENTS

Every implemented component must register metadata.

Example:

```js
{
  id: "search-input",
  name: "SearchInput",
  level: "molecule",
  category: "input",
  description: "...",
  importPath: "@/ui/molecules/search-input",
  tags: ["search", "input", "filter"],
  capabilities: [
    "input",
    "interactive"
  ],
  variants: [],
  slots: [],
  dependencies: ["input", "icon-button"],
  interactive: true,
  responsive: true,
  status: "experimental",
  componentVersion: "0.1.0"
}

```

Metadata must reflect reality.

Do not blindly copy the same capabilities into every component.

---

# 45. DEPENDENCY VALIDATION

Maintain direction:

```text
primitive
↓
atom
↓
molecule
↓
organism

```

No upward dependency.

Examples:

```text
atom → organism

```

is invalid.

```text
molecule → template

```

is invalid.

Registry validation should catch architectural dependency violations where practical.

---

# 46. REGISTRY DISCOVERY

By the end of this phase, basic discovery helpers should be possible.

Examples:

```js
findComponents({
  level: "atom"
})

```

```js
findComponents({
  category: "navigation"
})

```

```js
findComponents({
  capabilities: ["input"]
})

```

Keep discovery deterministic and simple.

Do NOT build embeddings/vector search.

---

# 47. COMPONENT MAP

Only implemented components enter:

```text
componentMap

```

Every `componentMap` entry must have metadata.

No planned-only component may be executable.

---

# 48. TOKENS ONLY

Do not introduce new page-level color systems.

New components must consume existing:

```text
semantic CSS variables
theme tokens
spacing rhythm
radius system
typography system
motion system

```

If a missing token is genuinely needed:

add it centrally.

Do NOT hardcode repeated arbitrary values.

---

# 49. THEME TESTING

All implemented components must remain functional under:

```text
default
obsidian
minimal
corporate
glass
futuristic
terminal

```

and supported color modes.

Do not create per-theme component forks.

---

# 50. RESPONSIVE REQUIREMENTS

Validate major organisms at:

```text
320
375
768
1024
1280
1440+

```

conceptually or through available preview tooling.

Especially inspect:

```text
Sidebar
DataTable
PageHeader
FilterBar
FormSection
MetricGrid

```

---

# 51. DENSITY

Where genuinely useful, support:

```text
comfortable
compact
dense

```

Prioritize:

```text
DataTable
Sidebar
navigation
forms
metric layouts

```

Do not expose density props where they serve no purpose.

---

# 52. ACCESSIBILITY

Audit:

```text
keyboard navigation
focus ring
screen-reader labels
form relationships
disabled states
ARIA semantics
dialogs/popovers
contrast
reduced motion

```

Icon-only controls must have accessible labels.

---

# 53. NO BUSINESS DATA

No hardcoded:

```text
users
companies
revenue
orders
servers
AI providers
customer names
currency totals

```

inside reusable source.

Fixtures/demos, if necessary, live outside production components.

---

# 54. NO BACKEND ACCESS

Search all new components for:

```text
fetch(
axios
graphql
database
supabase
firebase
odoo
server actions

```

Reusable components must not depend on them.

---

# 55. NO NEXT.JS COUPLING

Core Crayon components should not directly depend on:

```text
next/navigation
next/router
next/link
next/image
server-only

```

unless an explicit adapter exists outside the reusable core.

---

# 56. JAVASCRIPT REQUIREMENT

New Crayon files:

```text
.js
.jsx

```

Do not generate:

```text
.ts
.tsx

```

Existing application TSX infrastructure may remain unchanged.

---

# 57. DEMO / CATALOG PREPARATION

Do not build the full component catalog yet.

However, create enough isolated usage examples/tests to verify components.

Do not pollute production component files with demo data.

The full catalog will be a later phase.

---

# 58. COMPONENT FAMILY AUDIT

Before creating each component family, ask:

```text
Does an existing component already solve this?
Can this be a variant?
Can this be composition?
Does this need a new component at all?

```

Examples:

Do NOT create:

```text
SuccessBadge
ErrorBadge
WarningBadge

```

if:

```jsx
<Badge variant="success" />

```

is sufficient.

Do NOT create:

```text
SidebarNavItem
TopNavItem
SettingsNavItem

```

if a coherent NavItem abstraction genuinely covers them.

But do not force unrelated interactions into one mega-component merely to reduce file count.

---

# 59. COMPONENT COMPLEXITY AUDIT

If a component accumulates:

```text
many unrelated responsibilities
large configuration surface
independent interaction systems
large repeated JSX sections

```

refactor it.

However:

do not split components into meaningless micro-files.

---

# 60. CODE QUALITY

Remove:

```text
unused imports
dead exports
console.log
temporary debug components
commented-out implementation
duplicate classes
copy-pasted variants

```

Prefer clear code over excessive comments.

---

# 61. OPTIONAL CVA

If the project already has a coherent variant utility such as:

```text
class-variance-authority

```

reuse it.

Do not introduce a second competing variant system.

If no such dependency is needed, avoid adding dependencies unnecessarily.

---

# 62. SAFE COMPOSITION

When registering components for Crayon renderer use explicit maps only.

Never:

```text
eval()
new Function()
dynamic import from schema value

```

Stable component IDs only.

---

# 63. FOUNDATION WARNING

There is currently a Node warning because package.json does not declare:

```json
"type": "module"

```

Do NOT change package module type merely to silence a harmless warning unless you have verified all Next.js/project tooling remains compatible.

Prefer to leave it alone if it does not affect correctness.

Do not create collateral breakage for cosmetic warning cleanup.

---

# 64. TESTING

Add meaningful tests or programmatic validation where the existing tooling supports it.

Priorities:

```text
Button variants
form accessibility relationships
registry synchronization
componentMap consistency
resolver behavior
theme compatibility
schema-safe components

```

Do not create huge volumes of meaningless snapshots.

---

# 65. REQUIRED FOUNDATION VALIDATION

Update:

```text
scripts/validate-foundation.mjs

```

or create an appropriately named expanded validation script.

It should now report actual counts such as:

```text
Primitives: X
Atoms: X
Molecules: X
Organisms: X

Metadata entries: X
Executable components: X

Stable: X
Experimental: X
Planned: X
Deprecated: X

```

Do not hardcode those counts.

Calculate them from actual registries/files.

---

# 66. REGISTRY INVARIANTS

Validate:

```text
every executable component has metadata
every executable ID is unique
every metadata ID is unique
planned components are non-executable
implemented dependencies exist
dependency hierarchy is legal
deprecated replacement exists when declared
no self-dependency
registry import paths are valid
status is valid
level is valid
category is valid
capabilities are valid

```

---

# 67. BUILD QUALITY GATE

Before finishing:

run the actual project validation.

At minimum:

```text
pnpm build

```

and the Crayon validation script.

If lint/test scripts exist, run relevant ones.

Do not claim a check passed unless it actually ran.

---

# 68. EXPECTED SCALE

Do NOT stop after implementing five components.

The phase should create a useful base library.

Aim approximately for:

```text
8–14 primitives
20–30 atoms
20–35 molecules
12–20 organisms

```

This is guidance, NOT a quota.

If two proposed components are redundant:

implement one better component rather than two duplicates.

A final total around:

```text
60–90 real reusable components

```

would be appropriate if the architecture supports it naturally.

Quality takes priority over numeric count.

---

# 69. DO NOT IMPLEMENT YET

Do NOT build substantial:

```text
CRM blocks
ERP blocks
AI blocks
Infrastructure blocks
Billing blocks
dashboard templates
application pages

```

during this phase.

Those belong to the next layer.

Core organisms may include generic DataTable/ActivityFeed/etc because future blocks will depend on them.

---

# 70. NEXT PHASE PREPARATION

The output of this phase must make Phase 7–9 straightforward:

```text
Phase 7
Domain Blocks

Phase 8
Layouts

Phase 9
Templates

```

At that point Crayon should be able to compose rich application interfaces without inventing primitive UI.

---

# 71. FINAL AUDIT

Before stopping, inspect the resulting project for:

```text
duplicate components
unregistered components
planned executable components
hardcoded colors
hardcoded business data
backend calls
TypeScript in new Crayon source
Next.js coupling
circular imports
invalid hierarchy dependencies
accessibility regressions
unused files
empty ceremonial folders

```

Fix issues wherever reasonably possible.

---

